The best way is to kill 'em all before you even go near the water. Use
telepathy to locate them, then attack with a ranged weapon. Projectiles
land in the water, so your best choice is an attack spell. Failing that,
use rocks, which can be acquired in arbitrary amounts (pickaxe a
boulder) and, when fired from a sling (as found on many dead hobbits),
do a measurable amount of damage. If you do get grabbed by a sea
creature, zap a wand of teleport at it. An oilskin cloak can prevent
grabbin, I don't think greased armor can. At least not very well.

